  "result": "I fixed an off-by-one in the project limit check, in `src/server/services/project-service.ts:50`. I haven't run the tests.\n\n**Cause:** Before creating a project, `createProject` calls `wouldExceedLimit(org.plan, \"projects\", used, 0)`. That function checks whether the current count plus the number being added goes over the limit. Passing `0` meant it only looked at the projects that already existed, not the one being created. An org sitting exactly at its limit therefore passed the check and got one more project. Only the attempt after that was refused, once the org was already over.\n\n**Fix:** The call now passes `1` for the project being created. A free-plan org with 2 of 2 projects is now refused on its third, instead of on its fourth.\n\n`tests/server/plan-limits.test.ts` has a test for this exact case (\"rejects the project that would exceed the plan\"). I haven't confirmed it passes now.",
